From 4109e18d5ae5e25c1a2e8e970827aac55605c98f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:36:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/23] avcodec: add native AC-4 decoder core

Vendored streaming decoder core (bit reader, entropy, IMDCT, QMF,
A-SPX, ACPL, channel/render logic, static tables). In-tree port of the
dec-lib snapshot: FFmpeg LGPL header prepend per file plus CLI/shim
strip in dec_lib.c (no main), environment-knob/file-dump/stderr-probe
strip (defaults pinned: M4 HF rolloff on, experimental curves off,
cached IMDCT kernels, hot-gap-fill on), in-tree allocator conversion
(av_malloc family, no unportable headers), and a comment scrub to
table/clause citations; the unreferenced stage-contract header is
dropped. Default behavior preserved. No lavc API surface yet: the
OBJS stanza sits under the not-yet-defined CONFIG_AC4_DECODER guard,
so this patch builds inert and the 2/2 wrapper flips the codec live.

Table files land as *_tab.c/h (in-tree ac3tab/aactab precedent): the
libavcodec/Makefile CLEANFILES = *_tables.c *_tables.h pattern (plus
the matching libavcodec/.gitignore lines) deletes committed
*_tables.c/h sources on 'make clean', so the dec-lib *_tables names
cannot land verbatim.

This is an independent cleanroom implementation written from ETSI
TS 103 190-1 V1.4.1 and TS 103 190-2 V1.3.1 plus black-box behavioral
observation. No Dolby SDK, reference code, or disassembly was used;
numeric codebook/coefficient tables are value-only transcriptions
from the ETSI deliverables. Note AC-4 is covered by Dolby patents;
this submission addresses copyright-clean code only and
implementers/distributors should consider patent licensing.

Signed-off-by: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
